§§ `נספח — פסקה 85.125 לתקשי"ר: דרגת פרישה`

-- akn:attachments The annexes: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p1 "The wording of paragraph 85.125 of the Takshir follows"; no rule of its own.

-- (א) (the heading: rules of entitlement to a retirement grade for those
-- entitled to a pension under the Pensions Law). 1. the qualifying events:
-- (א) retiring on a pension at 60 or over; (ב) retiring on a pension for
-- reasons of health (medical unfitness), at any age; (ג) dying in service,
-- at any age, so that the survivors are entitled to a pension.
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1__para_a akn:att_1__hc_1__para_a__subpara_1 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_a__subpara_1__cls_a akn:att_1__hc_1__para_a__subpara_1__cls_b akn:att_1__hc_1__para_a__subpara_1__cls_c
DECLARE `retirement-grade event` IS ONE OF
    `retiring on a pension at 60 or over`
    `retiring on a pension for reasons of health`
    `dying in service, the survivors entitled to a pension`
    `retiring on a pension under 60, not for health`

GIVEN e IS A `retirement-grade event`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a qualifying event for a retirement grade` e IF
    NOT e EQUALS `retiring on a pension under 60, not for health`

@desc An employee at a qualifying event, as paragraph 85.125 of the Takshir asks.
DECLARE `retirement-grade case` HAS
    `the retirement-grade event of the case`                                   IS A `retirement-grade event`
    `in a scale the retirement-grade rules apply to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (א)3א's list
    `in a scale (א)3ג lets in by the grade span alone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc social workers, radiographers, physiotherapists, nurses, doctors, paramedical staff, occupational therapists
    `entitled to a retirement grade under another arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years of pensionable service at the event`   IS A NUMBER
    `years in his grade at the event`             IS A NUMBER
    `has a stay supplement in his grade`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `in a post with a grade span or a promotion track, below its peak` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the share of his grade's stay period completed` IS A NUMBER
    `in an open standard`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `an outstanding employee the Commissioner approved` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a bereaved parent or widow recognised by the law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in a scale the bereaved family's rule lists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (ב)ד1's longer list
    `half-steps from his place to the top grade's` IS A NUMBER @desc a grade is two half-steps, a stay supplement one; to the scale's top grade with no stay supplement

-- 2. (the rules of entitlement, ¶2) the promotion is in the power of the
-- one responsible in the ministry or unit, on the superior's
-- recommendation, subject to: (א) the promotion is limited to one grade
-- below the scale's top grade, a stay supplement included — read as that
-- grade with its stay supplement, one half-step below the top; (ב) it
-- reaches one given a personal grade above his post's peak; (ג) the times
-- of (ב) below are not shortened, by a second degree or studies among
-- them; (ד) it is approved from the first of the month of the retirement or
-- death.
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1__para_a__subpara_1__cls_c/p2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_a__subpara_1__cls_c/p3 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_a__subpara_1__cls_c__pnt_a akn:att_1__hc_1__para_a__subpara_1__cls_c__pnt_b akn:att_1__hc_1__para_a__subpara_1__cls_c__pnt_c akn:att_1__hc_1__para_a__subpara_1__cls_c__pnt_d
GIVEN `the half-steps the criteria give` IS A NUMBER, `half-steps from his place to the top grade's` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the half-steps a retirement promotion may add` `the half-steps the criteria give` `half-steps from his place to the top grade's` IS
    min `the half-steps the criteria give` (`not below zero` (`half-steps from his place to the top grade's` MINUS 1))

`a retirement promotion takes effect from the first of the month of the event` MEANS TRUE
`a retirement promotion's times may be shortened` MEANS FALSE

-- (ה): for one facing disciplinary proceedings, or whose proceedings dealt
-- with the end of his service, the promotion follows consultation with the
-- deputy Civil Service Commissioner for discipline.
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1__para_a__subpara_1__cls_c__pnt_e
GIVEN `disciplinary proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `2008 framework action`
DECIDE `consulting on discipline before a retirement promotion` `disciplinary proceedings` IS
    IF `disciplinary proceedings`
    THEN PARTY `the employer`
         MUST  `consult the deputy commissioner for discipline on a retirement promotion`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- 3. (the heading: entitlement by scale). (א) the rules reach the scales:
-- administrative, academics in the social sciences and humanities,
-- journalists, engineers, practical engineers, technicians, jurists, state
-- attorneys, the prison service's civilian staff, pharmacists, medical
-- technicians and scientists, the foreign service; (ב) not other scales —
-- teaching employees, research workers and those on senior contracts with
-- a budgetary pension among them; nor the civil administration of Judea
-- and Samaria and Gaza, the security service, the Mossad and Nativ; (ג) nor
-- social workers, radiographers, physiotherapists, nurses, doctors,
-- paramedical staff and occupational therapists — save that one of them,
-- at a qualifying event, in a post with a grade span, level of role
-- allowance or promotion track, below its peak, who has completed at least
-- half his grade's stay period, is promoted one grade; (ד) nor one entitled
-- to a retirement grade by another arrangement. A closed list each
-- (convention reading.closed-list).
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1__para_a__subpara_1__cls_c__hc_1 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_a__subpara_1__cls_c__hc_1__pnt_a akn:att_1__hc_1__para_a__subpara_1__cls_c__hc_1__pnt_a/p2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_a__subpara_1__cls_c__hc_1__pnt_b akn:att_1__hc_1__para_a__subpara_1__cls_c__hc_1__pnt_b/p2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_a__subpara_1__cls_c__hc_1__pnt_b/p3 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_a__subpara_1__cls_c__hc_1__pnt_b/p4 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_a__subpara_1__cls_c__hc_1__pnt_c akn:att_1__hc_1__para_a__subpara_1__cls_c__hc_1__pnt_c/p2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_a__subpara_1__cls_c__hc_1__pnt_c/p3 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_a__subpara_1__cls_c__hc_1__pnt_d
`the scales the retirement-grade rules apply to` MEANS
    LIST "מינהלי", "מח\"ר", "עיתונאים", "מהנדסים", "הנדסאים", "טכנאים", "משפטנים", "פרקליטים", "בכ\"מ", "רוקחים", "מקצ\"ט", "שירות החוץ"

`the scales (א)3ג lets in by the grade span alone` MEANS
    LIST "עובדים סוציאליים", "רנטגנאים", "פיזיוטרפיסטים", "אחיות", "רופאים", "פארה רפואיים", "מרפאים בעיסוק"

-- The grade-span rule: below the post's peak, at least half the stay
-- period done — the grade above (two half-steps).
GIVEN c IS A `retirement-grade case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the grade-span rule promotes him` c IF
        c's `in a post with a grade span or a promotion track, below its peak`
    AND c's `the share of his grade's stay period completed` AT LEAST 50%

-- akn:att_1__hc_1__para_a__subpara_1__cls_c__hc_1__pnt_d/p2 A page number; no rule.

-- (ב) (the heading: the criteria for one retiring for age or health): one
-- in a scale of (א)3א retiring at 60 or over, or at any age for health
-- (unfitness a medical committee for state employees found), has his
-- retirement grade set by one of these. 1. short of 40 pensionable years:
-- (א) three years in his grade, no stay supplement — the grade above; (ב)
-- three years with a stay supplement — the grade above, with a stay
-- supplement; (ג) one year in his grade — a stay supplement; (ד) one year
-- with a stay supplement — the grade above, without one; (ה) in a post
-- with a grade span or promotion track, below its peak, at least half the
-- stay period done — the grade above (not in an open standard). 2. with 40
-- pensionable years or more: (א)–(ב) a year in his grade — the grade
-- above (with a stay supplement where he had one); (ג)–(ד) less than a
-- year — a stay supplement, or the grade above without one where he had
-- one. In half-steps: under 40 years, three years add two and one year
-- one; at 40, a year adds two and less adds one. Where two of a list's
-- alternatives fit (three years are also one), the one that gives more is
-- read (convention amounts.highest).
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b/p2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1__cls_a akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1__cls_b akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1__cls_c akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1__cls_d akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1__cls_e akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1__cls_e/p2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1__cls_e__pnt_a akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1__cls_e__pnt_b akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1__cls_e__pnt_c akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1__cls_e__pnt_d
GIVEN c IS A `retirement-grade case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the half-steps (ב)1–2 give` c IS
    IF c's `years of pensionable service at the event` AT LEAST 40
    THEN (IF c's `years in his grade at the event` AT LEAST 1 THEN 2 ELSE 1)
    ELSE max (IF c's `years in his grade at the event` AT LEAST 3
              THEN 2
              ELSE IF c's `years in his grade at the event` AT LEAST 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0)
             (IF `the grade-span rule promotes him` c AND NOT c's `in an open standard` THEN 2 ELSE 0)

-- 3. an outstanding employee with 40 pensionable years or more: the
-- director-general or the head of a unit may recommend, with reasons, a
-- promotion for lasting personal and professional excellence, approved by
-- the Civil Service Commissioner: (א) three years in his grade, no stay
-- supplement — the grade above with a stay supplement ("a grade and a
-- half"); (ב) three years with a stay supplement — the grade above and one
-- more, without a stay supplement (again "a grade and a half"): three
-- half-steps.
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1__cls_e__pnt_d/p2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1__cls_e__pnt_d/p3 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1__cls_e__pnt_d/p4 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1__cls_e__pnt_d__pnt_a akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1__cls_e__pnt_d__pnt_b
GIVEN c IS A `retirement-grade case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the half-steps (ב)3 gives` c IS
    IF      c's `an outstanding employee the Commissioner approved`
        AND c's `years of pensionable service at the event` AT LEAST 40
        AND c's `years in his grade at the event` AT LEAST 3
    THEN 3
    ELSE 0

-- (ג) death in service: 1. one in a scale of (א)3א who dies in service, at
-- any age, his survivors entitled to a pension, has his retirement grade
-- set however long he was in his grade: (א) with no stay supplement, the
-- grade above; (ב) with one, the grade above with a stay supplement — two
-- half-steps either way. 2. an outstanding employee who dies with 40
-- pensionable years, by (ב)3.
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1__cls_e__pnt_d__pnt_c akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1__cls_e__pnt_d__pnt_c__pnt_1 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1__cls_e__pnt_d__pnt_c__pnt_1__pnt_a akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1__cls_e__pnt_d__pnt_c__pnt_1__pnt_b akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1__cls_e__pnt_d__pnt_c__pnt_2
GIVEN c IS A `retirement-grade case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the half-steps (ג) gives on a death in service` c IS
    max 2 (`the half-steps (ב)3 gives` c)

-- akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1__cls_e__pnt_d__pnt_c__pnt_1/p2 A page number; no rule.

-- (ד) a bereaved parent or a widow(er) recognised under the Fallen
-- Soldiers' Families Law, 1950 or the Victims of Hostile Action Law, 1970:
-- 1. one in the scales it lists (those of (א)3א, the research workers, and
-- those of (א)3ג, and the civil administration's) is promoted a further
-- retirement grade, beside his promotion by (ב) and (ג), limited too to
-- one grade below the top with a stay supplement; 2. the events: retiring
-- on a pension at any age, or dying in service with survivors entitled to
-- a pension; 3. from the first of the month of the event; 4. approved by
-- the senior division manager for retirement terms, pensions and welfare
-- at the Civil Service Commission.
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1__cls_e__pnt_d__pnt_d akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1__cls_e__pnt_d__pnt_d__pnt_1 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1__cls_e__pnt_d__pnt_d__pnt_2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1__cls_e__pnt_d__pnt_d__pnt_2__pnt_a akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1__cls_e__pnt_d__pnt_d__pnt_2__pnt_b akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1__cls_e__pnt_d__pnt_d__pnt_3 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1__cls_e__pnt_d__pnt_d__pnt_4
GIVEN c IS A `retirement-grade case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the half-steps (ד) adds for a bereaved family` c IS
    IF c's `a bereaved parent or widow recognised by the law` AND c's `in a scale the bereaved family's rule lists`
    THEN 2
    ELSE 0

`who approves a bereaved family's retirement grade` MEANS `the Civil Service Commission`

-- The retirement promotion, in half-steps: none without a qualifying event
-- or under another arrangement; (א)3ג's scales by the grade span alone;
-- (א)3א's by (ב) or (ג); (ד) on top for a bereaved family; capped by 2(א).
GIVEN c IS A `retirement-grade case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the retirement promotion in half-steps` c IS
    IF c's `entitled to a retirement grade under another arrangement`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the half-steps a retirement promotion may add`
             (BRANCH
                 IF c's `the retirement-grade event of the case` EQUALS `retiring on a pension under 60, not for health`
                 THEN `the half-steps (ד) adds for a bereaved family` c
                 IF c's `in a scale the retirement-grade rules apply to`
                 THEN (IF c's `the retirement-grade event of the case` EQUALS `dying in service, the survivors entitled to a pension`
                       THEN `the half-steps (ג) gives on a death in service` c
                       ELSE max (`the half-steps (ב)1–2 give` c) (`the half-steps (ב)3 gives` c))
                      PLUS `the half-steps (ד) adds for a bereaved family` c
                 IF c's `in a scale (א)3ג lets in by the grade span alone`
                 THEN (IF `the grade-span rule promotes him` c THEN 2 ELSE 0)
                      PLUS `the half-steps (ד) adds for a bereaved family` c
                 OTHERWISE `the half-steps (ד) adds for a bereaved family` c)
             (c's `half-steps from his place to the top grade's`)

§§ `findings`

-- F-framework-2008-a: three cross-references name the section before the
-- one they mean — §3 and the paragraph after 16.2(ג) name §8 for the
-- negotiation of §9, and 12.4 names §10 for the amendment of §11.
`the section §3 and §16.2 name for the agreements still to be signed` MEANS 8
`the section that provides for those agreements` MEANS 9
`the section 12.4 names for the first amendment` MEANS 10
`the section that sets out the first amendment` MEANS 11

`three of the 2008 framework's cross-references name the section before the one they mean` MEANS
        `the section §3 and §16.2 name for the agreements still to be signed` EQUALS `the section that provides for those agreements` MINUS 1
    AND `the section 12.4 names for the first amendment` EQUALS `the section that sets out the first amendment` MINUS 1

#ASSERT `three of the 2008 framework's cross-references name the section before the one they mean`

-- F-framework-2008-b: supplement B for one who retired in 2008 runs from
-- December 2007's index to his last month of work's, and his yearly
-- updates start from December 2008's index ((ה)(1)), so the months between
-- his retirement and December 2008 enter neither. A pensioner who retired
-- on 31.12.2007 has the year's rise less 0.25%; one who retired on
-- 1.1.2008 (his last month of work December 2007) has none; one who
-- retired in December 2008, active the whole year, has all of it. Indices
-- of 100 and 104 are placeholders.
`a pensioner who retired on 31.12.2007` MEANS `supplement B case` WITH
    `the year he retired in, for B`        IS 2007
    `the index of December 2007, for B`           IS 100
    `the index of December 2008, for B`    IS 104
    `the index of his last month of work, for B` IS 100
`a pensioner who retired on 1.1.2008` MEANS `supplement B case` WITH
    `the year he retired in, for B`        IS 2008
    `the index of December 2007, for B`           IS 100
    `the index of December 2008, for B`    IS 104
    `the index of his last month of work, for B` IS 100
`a pensioner who retired on 31.12.2008` MEANS `supplement B case` WITH
    `the year he retired in, for B`        IS 2008
    `the index of December 2007, for B`           IS 100
    `the index of December 2008, for B`    IS 104
    `the index of his last month of work, for B` IS 104

`supplement B gives a retiree of 1.1.2008 none of the 2008 rise that one of 31.12.2007 has` MEANS
        `supplement B's rate` `a pensioner who retired on 1.1.2008` EQUALS 0
    AND `supplement B's rate` `a pensioner who retired on 31.12.2007` GREATER THAN 3%
    AND `supplement B's rate` `a pensioner who retired on 31.12.2008` GREATER THAN `supplement B's rate` `a pensioner who retired on 31.12.2007`

#ASSERT `supplement B gives a retiree of 1.1.2008 none of the 2008 rise that one of 31.12.2007 has`

§§ `illustrations`

-- §3 and the law's §§15–16: a nurse of the State is covered; a teaching
-- employee of the State is not, under either kind of agreement.
`a nurse of the State in 2009` MEANS `2008 framework employee` WITH
    `employed by an employer that signed the 2008 framework` IS TRUE
    `his pay is computed by the agreements of a scale the Histadrut represents` IS TRUE
    `employed in the month the 2008 payment is made for` IS TRUE
`a teaching employee of the State in 2009` MEANS `2008 framework employee` WITH
    `employed by an employer that signed the 2008 framework` IS TRUE
    `his pay is computed by the agreements of a scale the Histadrut represents` IS FALSE
    `employed in the month the 2008 payment is made for` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `the 2008 framework agreement covers` `a nurse of the State in 2009`
#ASSERT NOT `the 2008 framework agreement covers` `a teaching employee of the State in 2009`
#ASSERT NOT `the collective agreement applies to the employee` `a general collective agreement` (`the 2008 framework employee, as the law asks` `a teaching employee of the State in 2009`)
#ASSERT NOT `the collective agreement applies to the employee` `a special collective agreement` (`the 2008 framework employee, as the law asks` `a teaching employee of the State in 2009`)
#ASSERT `the collective agreement applies to the employee` `a special collective agreement` (`the 2008 framework employee, as the law asks` `a nurse of the State in 2009`)
#ASSERT count `the employers that signed the 2008 framework` EQUALS 13

-- §4: 1.5% in 2008, 3% from December 2008, 5% from December 2009 on; in
-- 2008 none of it is a rise in monthly pay. The month form agrees with the
-- day form.
#ASSERT `the 2008 framework cost frame on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2007) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the 2008 framework cost frame on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 11 2008) EQUALS 1.5%
#ASSERT `the 2008 framework cost frame on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2008) EQUALS 3%
#ASSERT `the 2008 framework cost frame on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2009) EQUALS 5%
#ASSERT `the 2008 framework cost frame on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2015) EQUALS 5%
#ASSERT `the 2008 framework frame allocated to monthly pay on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2008) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the 2008 framework cost frame in the salary month` (`the 2008 framework month` 2009 11) EQUALS 3%
#ASSERT `the 2008 framework cost frame in the salary month` (`the 2008 framework month` 2009 12) EQUALS 5%
#ASSERT `the 2008 framework cost frame of the local authorities on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2010) (0.5%) EQUALS 4.5%
#ASSERT NOT `the 2008 framework may pay for work done on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 11 2008) FALSE
#ASSERT `the 2008 framework may pay for work done on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 11 2008) TRUE

-- §5: overtime and a derived yearly grant are in the base; a supplement
-- with a mechanism of its own, a minimum-wage top-up and an expense
-- reimbursement are not.
`overtime of the 2008 base` MEANS `2008 framework pay component` WITH
    `the 2008 component's kind` IS `overtime, shifts, duty, standby, call-outs or incentive pay of the 2008 base`
    `the 2008 component is paid monthly, weekly or daily` IS TRUE
    `the 2008 component is updated by the cost-of-living agreements` IS FALSE
    `the 2008 component is a minimum-wage top-up` IS FALSE
`a supplement with a mechanism of its own` MEANS `2008 framework pay component` WITH
    `the 2008 component's kind` IS `another supplement in shekels or in percent of the 2008 base`
    `the 2008 component is paid monthly, weekly or daily` IS TRUE
    `the 2008 component is updated by the cost-of-living agreements` IS FALSE
    `the 2008 component is a minimum-wage top-up` IS FALSE
`a minimum-wage top-up of the 2008 base` MEANS `2008 framework pay component` WITH
    `the 2008 component's kind` IS `another supplement in shekels or in percent of the 2008 base`
    `the 2008 component is paid monthly, weekly or daily` IS TRUE
    `the 2008 component is updated by the cost-of-living agreements` IS TRUE
    `the 2008 component is a minimum-wage top-up` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `in the base of the 2008 framework cost frame` `overtime of the 2008 base`
#ASSERT NOT `in the base of the 2008 framework cost frame` `a supplement with a mechanism of its own`
#ASSERT NOT `in the base of the 2008 framework cost frame` `a minimum-wage top-up of the 2008 base`
#ASSERT `the 2008 framework salary base from` (LIST 9000, 9000, 9000, 9000, 9000, 9000, 11000, 11000, 11000, 11000, 11000, 11000) EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `the employer §6 computes the 2008 cost for` (`another employer of the 2008 framework` "שלוש הערים הגדולות") EQUALS "שלוש הערים הגדולות"
#ASSERT NOT `a 2008 framework supplement counts for the minimum-wage top-up` FALSE

-- §8: the multiplier is eleven months of 1.5%; averages of 9,000 and 1,000
-- give a grant of 1,650 for the whole period and 825 for half of it; paid
-- 1,650 for half, 825 is an advance to deduct; a component's year of
-- 120,000 is 10,000 a month, 6 months' 54,000 is 9,000. One who joined and
-- left in October 2008 is paid with November's salary.
#ASSERT `the 2008 grant's multiplier` EQUALS 11 TIMES 1.5%
#ASSERT `the 2008 one-time grant` (LIST 9000, 1000) 11 EQUALS 1650
#ASSERT `the 2008 one-time grant` (LIST 9000, 1000) 5.5 EQUALS 825
#ASSERT `the 2008 one-time grant` (LIST 9000, 1000) 12 EQUALS 1650
#ASSERT `the advance of the 2008 grant to deduct` 1650 825 EQUALS 825
#ASSERT `the 2008 grant's average of a component` 120000 12 EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `the 2008 grant's average of a component` 54000 6 EQUALS 9000
#ASSERT `the months that count as actual work for the 2008 grant` 9 1 1 EQUALS 11
#ASSERT `the salary month a later-joining employee is paid the 2008 grant with` (JUST (`the 2008 framework month` 2008 10)) EQUALS `the 2008 framework month` 2008 11
#ASSERT `the salary month a later-joining employee is paid the 2008 grant with` NOTHING EQUALS `the 2008 framework month` 2008 12
#ASSERT `the provident-fund contribution on the 2008 grant for a component` 10000 (6%) 11 EQUALS 99
#ASSERT `the 2008 grant counts for` `provident-fund contributions, of the 2008 grant`
#ASSERT NOT `the 2008 grant counts for` `severance pay, of the 2008 grant`

-- §§9–10: a scale with no agreement by 30.11.2008 goes to decision; an
-- agreement signed on 10.3.2009 pays from March's salary (by April's), one
-- of 11.3.2009 from April's (by May's), with differences for the months
-- from December 2008.
#ASSERT `the scale goes to the wages commissioner and the Histadrut's chair` NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `the scale goes to the wages commissioner and the Histadrut's chair` (JUST (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 11 2008))
#ASSERT `the salary month a 2008 section 9 agreement is paid from` 10 3 2009 EQUALS `the 2008 framework month` 2009 3
#ASSERT `the latest salary month a 2008 section 9 agreement is paid from` 11 3 2009 EQUALS `the 2008 framework month` 2009 5
#ASSERT `the months of differences from 1.12.2008` (`the 2008 framework month` 2009 4) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT NOT `a 2008 section 9 agreement may pay on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 11 2008)
#ASSERT `the frame a 2008 section 9 agreement allocates on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2009) EQUALS 3%

-- §11: a determining salary of 1,000 last set at an index of 100 rises to
-- 1,100 on 110, stays through a fall to 99, and rises to 1,210 on 121 —
-- the fall counted in full. December 2008's index is the base for one
-- whose pension began by then.
#ASSERT `the determining salary after the yearly index updates` 1000 100 (LIST 110, 99, 121) EQUALS 1210
#ASSERT `the determining salary after the yearly index updates` 1000 100 (LIST 99, 98) EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `the base index of his first update` (`the 2008 framework month` 2008 12) 95 100 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `the base index of his first update` (`the 2008 framework month` 2009 6) 102 100 EQUALS 102

-- Supplement A's table holds to itself: each row's last step is its final
-- rate, and the steps never fall. A 2003 retiree: 5% from July 2008, 9%
-- from April 2009, still 9% in 2010; one of 1998 reads the first row.
GIVEN r IS A `supplement A row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `supplement A's row reaches its final rate` r IF
    `supplement A's rate after the step` (r's `supplement A's rate from April 2010`)
        (`supplement A's rate after the step` (r's `supplement A's rate from April 2009`) (r's `supplement A's rate from July 2008`))
    EQUALS r's `supplement A's final rate`

#ASSERT all `supplement A's row reaches its final rate` `supplement A's table`
#ASSERT `supplement A's rate` 2003 (`the 2008 framework month` 2008 7) EQUALS 5%
#ASSERT `supplement A's rate` 2003 (`the 2008 framework month` 2009 4) EQUALS 9%
#ASSERT `supplement A's rate` 2003 (`the 2008 framework month` 2010 6) EQUALS 9%
#ASSERT `supplement A's rate` 1998 (`the 2008 framework month` 2010 6) EQUALS 12%
#ASSERT `supplement A's rate` 2008 (`the 2008 framework month` 2010 6) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `supplement A` 2001 (`the 2008 framework month` 2010 4) 5000 180 EQUALS 569.8
#ASSERT `the rate supplement B takes off the index` 1995 EQUALS 0.6%
#ASSERT `supplement B` `a pensioner who retired on 31.12.2007` 1000 EQUALS 37.5
#ASSERT `supplement C's rate` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 11 2008) (`the 2008 framework month` 2009 12) EQUALS 5%
#ASSERT `supplement C's rate` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2008) (`the 2008 framework month` 2009 6) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `supplement C's rate` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2008) (`the 2008 framework month` 2009 12) EQUALS 2%
#ASSERT `supplement C's rate` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2009) (`the 2008 framework month` 2010 1) EQUALS 0
-- Supplement C keeps a pensioner level with the active rise: one who
-- retired by 30.11.2008 has the frame's 3% and 5%; one who retired in the
-- next year, active at the 3% step, has the 2% to 5%.
#ASSERT `supplement C's rate` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2008) (`the 2008 framework month` 2009 12) EQUALS `the 2008 framework cost frame on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2009)
#ASSERT `supplement C's rate` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2009) (`the 2008 framework month` 2009 12) EQUALS `the 2008 framework cost frame on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2009) MINUS `the 2008 framework cost frame on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2008)
#ASSERT `the month a §17א pensioner's supplement starts` 24100 24103 EQUALS 24103
#ASSERT `how an employer's arrangement updates the determining salary on` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2008) EQUALS `by the mechanism of the Pensions Law`
#ASSERT `how an employer's arrangement updates the determining salary on` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 11 2008) EQUALS `by an active employee's salary`
#ASSERT NOT `a determining salary follows active pay on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2009)
#ASSERT NOT `section 11 of the 2008 framework reaches the pensioner` TRUE

-- §12: 393 for each of three pensioners, one for half the year; updated by
