-- §16: a claim for 2008 is exhausted; one pending in arbitration is not.
#ASSERT `the 2008 framework exhausts the claim` FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2008)
#ASSERT NOT `the 2008 framework exhausts the claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2008)

-- The annex: an administrative employee retiring at 62, 30 years' service,
-- three years in his grade, four half-steps below the top, goes up a grade;
-- with 40 years and a year in his grade, a grade; outstanding, a grade and
-- a half; one half-step below the top, nothing; a nurse below her post's
-- peak with half its stay done, a grade; a teaching employee, nothing.
`an administrative employee retiring at 62` MEANS `retirement-grade case` WITH
    `the retirement-grade event of the case`                                   IS `retiring on a pension at 60 or over`
    `in a scale the retirement-grade rules apply to` IS TRUE
    `in a scale (א)3ג lets in by the grade span alone` IS FALSE
    `entitled to a retirement grade under another arrangement` IS FALSE
    `years of pensionable service at the event`   IS 30
    `years in his grade at the event`             IS 3
    `has a stay supplement in his grade`          IS FALSE
    `in a post with a grade span or a promotion track, below its peak` IS FALSE
    `the share of his grade's stay period completed` IS 0
    `in an open standard`                         IS FALSE
